annel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Handling of Missing and Overlapping Prices with Enable Tolerant Price Handling Flag in Configure Omnichannel Promotion Pricing App\nDescription: You can now use a new flag Enable Tolerant Price Handling in the Configure Omnichannel Promotion Pricing application to facilitate the handling of missing and overlapping prices for calculation in the line item mode.  For more information, see Enabling Tolerant Price Handling in Line Item Mode.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3042 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Handling of Sales and Returns without the Original Transaction\nDescription: The Handling of Sales and Returns without the Original Transaction has been enhanced. You can now maintain the field Calculation Base Type on the Promotional Rules detail page in the Maintain Promotions app. Additionally, the new transaction type ReturnTransaction has been added and is available as of Client API version 14.0.  For more information, see Handling of Sales and Returns without the Original Transaction.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3043 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Increasing of Maximum Number of Generic Attributes in Calculation Request\nDescription: The maximum number of generic attributes (generic transaction attribute and generic line item attribute) allowed in a calculation request has been increased from 10 to 20. For more information, see Security.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n-